WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:01:07.429 --> 00:01:10.262
(uplifting music)

00:01:21.616 --> 00:01:25.699
- [Jane Goodall] We're
all part of one community.

00:01:49.141 --> 00:01:50.299
- Hi everyone.

00:01:50.299 --> 00:01:52.057
I'm Jessica Nabongo coming to you

00:01:52.057 --> 00:01:54.041
from the National Geographic headquarters

00:01:54.041 --> 00:01:55.719
in Washington, D.C.

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:57.641
For over 130 years,

00:01:57.641 --> 00:02:00.295
Nat Geo has used its
groundbreaking storytelling

00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:03.661
to inspire the explorer
in everyone, including me.

00:02:03.661 --> 00:02:06.913
In October 2019, I became
the first black woman

00:02:06.913 --> 00:02:09.613
to visit every country in the world.

00:02:09.613 --> 00:02:12.449
Travel has helped me
better understand the world

00:02:12.449 --> 00:02:13.929
and my place in it.

00:02:13.929 --> 00:02:15.878
But when traveling isn't possible,

00:02:15.878 --> 00:02:18.842
Nat Geo helps us all
explore the furthest reaches

00:02:18.842 --> 00:02:20.949
of the Earth and beyond.

00:02:20.949 --> 00:02:23.601
Tonight I am happy to serve as your guide

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:26.226
as we embark on a musical
journey that will take us

00:02:26.226 --> 00:02:29.685
from the woodlands of Norway
to the coast of California.

00:02:29.685 --> 00:02:32.531
We have an incredible
Earth Day Eve lineup ahead

00:02:32.531 --> 00:02:35.620
with uplifting musical
performances by some

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.052
of our favorite planet-loving
artists alongside shout-outs

00:02:39.052 --> 00:02:41.992
from beloved National
Geographic Explorers.

00:02:41.992 --> 00:02:45.136
The party continues afterwards
on Nat Geo's TikTok.

00:02:45.136 --> 00:02:48.790
All of this as we count
down to Earth Day 2021

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.226
and the world premiere

00:02:50.226 --> 00:02:52.867
of "Secrets of the Whales" on Disney+.

00:02:52.867 --> 00:02:56.286
In a moment, singer-songwriter
Alt Bloom will tell you

00:02:56.286 --> 00:02:58.108
how you can be part of Share Your Spot,

00:02:58.108 --> 00:03:01.129
Nat Geo's Earth Day hashtag challenge.

00:03:01.129 --> 00:03:04.301
So kickback and get ready
to celebrate our shared love

00:03:04.301 --> 00:03:06.968
for the planet we all call home.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.622
- [Alt Bloom] Where is your favorite spot?

00:03:11.622 --> 00:03:14.808
That spot where our planet
feels most like home,

00:03:14.808 --> 00:03:16.975
where you feel most alive,

00:03:17.886 --> 00:03:22.303
most hopeful, most connected
to our world and others.

00:03:23.658 --> 00:03:26.323
National Geographic wants you
to share your favorite spot

00:03:26.323 --> 00:03:28.073
using #shareyourspot.

00:03:29.018 --> 00:03:30.006
We may even share it

00:03:30.006 --> 00:03:32.159
with our hundreds of
millions of followers,

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:34.478
a growing movement of
people who love our planet

00:03:34.478 --> 00:03:36.166
as much as you do.

00:03:36.166 --> 00:03:38.499
Join us and share your spot.

00:03:39.812 --> 00:03:43.619
- Hi, I'm Aurora and I think
it's fantastic to be here

00:03:43.619 --> 00:03:47.455
with you on National
Geographic Earth Day Eve.

00:03:47.455 --> 00:03:52.422
I especially love being here
because the matter of nature

00:03:52.422 --> 00:03:55.816
and the Earth is such an
important cause for me.

00:03:55.816 --> 00:03:58.684
It lies so close to my heart.

00:03:58.684 --> 00:04:02.064
For me, nature is definitely
the biggest source

00:04:02.064 --> 00:04:03.314
of inspiration.

00:04:04.442 --> 00:04:07.428
And it's the only place
I feel like I can go

00:04:07.428 --> 00:04:10.341
where no one ever asks you of anything.

00:04:10.341 --> 00:04:13.686
You can just purely exist out here

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.842
which I really, really love.

00:04:15.842 --> 00:04:18.739
This forest is a forest
that means a lot to me.

00:04:18.739 --> 00:04:21.279
I spent a lot of time here as a child,

00:04:21.279 --> 00:04:24.188
and it's very nice to be back.

00:04:24.188 --> 00:04:25.855
I feel very at home.

